{% doc %}
  blocks/_testimonial-intro.liquid — private to `sections/testimonials.liquid`.

  The filled panel at the head of the row: a line about the reviews, and the
  numbers that back it up.

  ## It is a static block, so it cannot be dragged into the carousel

  `sections/testimonials.liquid` renders it through
  `{% content_for 'block', type: '_testimonial-intro', id: 'testimonials-intro' %}`,
  the same mechanism `sections/feature-cards.liquid` uses for its heading
  cluster and for the same reason: it is part of the section's layout rather
  than one of its slides. A merchant editing it on the canvas cannot reorder it
  among the reviews, cannot delete it by accident, and cannot end up with two.

  It is also outside the `<swiper-carousel>` entirely. Inside the track it would
  be a slide — it would scroll away with the first arrow press, and Swiper would
  count it when deciding whether the merchant's Loop setting is achievable.

  ## The stats are blocks, and the heading is a setting

  The heading is one line that every panel has. The stats are a list whose
  length is content — two numbers here, one or three somewhere else — so they
  are `_testimonial-stat` blocks the merchant adds, reorders and removes.

  `@theme` is accepted alongside them, so a panel that wants a button under its
  numbers, or a logo above them, does not need this file changed.

  ## The panel paints itself rather than taking a colour scheme

  A colour scheme would be the theme's usual answer and it is the wrong one
  here: this panel is the *inverse* of the section it sits in — dark on light —
  and reaching for a second scheme to express that means a merchant who
  recolours the section has to remember to recolour a scheme they did not know
  was involved. A background and a text colour on the block say what they do.

  The section's own `--tc-accent` still reaches the stats, so the numbers stay
  in step with the heading's highlight above without either knowing about the
  other.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign align = s.alignment | default: 'start'
  assign gap = s.gap | default: 20 | plus: 0
  assign min_height = s.min_height | default: 366 | plus: 0
  assign width = s.width | default: 312 | plus: 0

  comment
    Same three-part border resolution as everything else in the theme —
    `sections/feature-cards.liquid`'s panel, `blocks/_feature-card.liquid`,
    `blocks/_testimonial-card.liquid`. One width rather than four: this panel is
    a filled box, and the frame a merchant wants around a filled box is the
    whole outline or nothing.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'
  assign border_width = 0
  assign border_paint = ''

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 20 | plus: 0
  assign radius_mobile = s.border_radius_mobile | default: radius | plus: 0

  comment
    The colour is only painted when there is no picture over it. A tint under a
    photograph that covers the panel is a colour nobody sees, and one under a
    *fitted* photograph is a second background fighting the overlay — which is
    the control that exists for exactly that job.
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false and s.background_color != blank
    assign background_alpha = s.background_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    assign background_alpha = background_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | color_modify: 'alpha', background_alpha
  endif
-%}

{%- capture intro_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --tc-intro-align: {{ align }};
  --tc-intro-gap: {{ gap }}px;
  --tc-intro-width: {{ width }}px;
  --tc-intro-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --tc-intro-radius-mobile: {{ radius_mobile }}px;
  --tc-intro-heading-size: {{ s.heading_size | default: 24 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --tc-intro-stat-gap: {{ s.stat_gap | default: 28 | plus: 0 }}px;
  {%- if min_height > 0 -%}
    --tc-intro-min-height: {{ min_height }}px;
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --tc-intro-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
    --tc-intro-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --tc-intro-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    --tc-intro-background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.text_color != blank -%}
    --tc-intro-text: {{ s.text_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="testimonial-intro{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-block-spacing
  style="{{ intro_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The same `snippets/background-media.liquid` every other surface in the theme
    uses, handed the block's own settings — so a picture, a video, the parallax
    and the overlay all arrive by adding settings rather than by adding markup
    here.

    `base.css` clips it to the panel's radius and lifts the heading and the stats
    above it. The snippet renders nothing at all when nothing is chosen, so the
    panel is not given a stacking context it has no use for.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      An `<h3>`, not an `<h2>`. The section's own heading cluster above is the
      `<h2>`, and this panel is a part of the row under it — promoting it would
      give the page two headings at the same level saying different things.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <h3 class="testimonial-intro__heading">{{ s.heading }}</h3>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The stats are pushed to the bottom of the panel by `margin-block-start: auto`
    in `base.css` rather than by a spacer here, so a panel taller than its
    content keeps the heading at the top and the numbers at the foot — which is
    what the design draws and what a fixed gap cannot hold at two viewport
    widths.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="testimonial-intro__stats">
    {% content_for 'blocks' %}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.name",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_testimonial-stat"
    },
    {
      "type": "@theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "t:shared.heading.label",
      "default": "See why our community loves us"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.settings.heading_size.label",
      "min": 16,
      "max": 56,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "width",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.settings.width.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.settings.width.info",
      "min": 200,
      "max": 560,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 312
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.min_height.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.settings.min_height.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 600,
      "step": 6,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 366
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.settings.gap.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 80,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "stat_gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.settings.stat_gap.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 28
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.appearance.background_color.label",
      "default": "#0F2E2F",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "background_opacity",
      "label": "t:sections.feature_cards.settings.panel_background_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "background_media",
      "label": "t:shared.background.media.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "image",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "video",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_position.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "cover",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fit",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "image_parallax",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_parallax.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_parallax.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "image_parallax_speed",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_parallax_speed.label",
      "min": 5,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 15,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'image' and block.settings.image_parallax }}",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_parallax_speed.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "video_url",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_url.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video_url.info",
      "accept": [
        "youtube",
        "vimeo"
      ],
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "video_poster",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_poster.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video_poster.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "video_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "cover",
          "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "contain",
          "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_loop",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_loop.label",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "overlay_enabled",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_enabled.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.overlay_enabled.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "overlay_style",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "solid",
          "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "gradient",
          "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "solid",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media != 'none' and block.settings.overlay_enabled }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "overlay_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_color.label",
      "default": "#000000",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media != 'none' and block.settings.overlay_enabled and block.settings.overlay_style == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "overlay_gradient",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_gradient.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.overlay_gradient.info",
      "default": "linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 40%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 1) 100%)",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media != 'none' and block.settings.overlay_enabled and block.settings.overlay_style == 'gradient' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "overlay_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 40,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_media != 'none' and block.settings.overlay_enabled }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_intro.settings.text_color.label",
      "default": "#FFFFFF"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.borders"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:shared.border.style.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.options.none"
        },
        {
          "value": "solid",
          "label": "t:shared.options.solid"
        },
        {
          "value": "dashed",
          "label": "t:shared.options.dashed"
        },
        {
          "value": "dotted",
          "label": "t:shared.border.style.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width",
